WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:04.900
There are many kinds of magic,

00:04.900 --> 00:09.160
but four are considered 
particularly important.

00:11.380 --> 00:15.780
Granting control to that nourishing 
force, the source of all life—

00:15.780 --> 00:16.990
the Sigil of Water.

00:18.890 --> 00:21.990
Turning stone to sand and sand to stone,

00:22.570 --> 00:26.170
enabling transformation and 
movement—the Sigil of Earth.

00:27.600 --> 00:30.280
That which frees us 
to visit distant realms,

00:30.280 --> 00:35.240
and has fueled so much progress—
the Sigil of Levitation.

00:36.720 --> 00:40.440
And that which has become 
humanity's sword and shield—

00:42.140 --> 00:43.530
the Sigil of Flame.

00:45.500 --> 00:50.760
Witches refer to these 
as the Primary Tetrad.

00:52.080 --> 00:55.490
So, let's give them a try.

01:16.720 --> 01:18.710
Wh-What do I do?!

01:23.060 --> 01:25.230
A-Are you all right?

01:25.230 --> 01:27.960
Thank you, Tetia...

01:27.960 --> 01:29.740
Thank you for thanking me!

01:29.740 --> 01:32.430
What were you doing, anyway?

01:32.430 --> 01:36.870
I was drawing the Pyreball spell as 
part of my levitation magic practice.

01:37.720 --> 01:41.200
The Sigil of Fire deals with formless 
phenomena, so it can be dangerous

01:41.200 --> 01:43.620
if it's not maintained at just 
the right size and balance.

01:43.620 --> 01:45.640
Be careful when you're using it.

01:45.640 --> 01:47.380
I will.

01:51.130 --> 01:54.480
I thought you'd mastered 
levitation magic at the Dadah Range.

01:54.480 --> 01:56.740
Why do you need to practice it now?

01:57.760 --> 02:00.600
You were out there 
zoom-zoom-zooming around!

02:00.600 --> 02:02.020
Zoomie-zoomie-zoom!

02:02.690 --> 02:08.000
I ruined the Sylph Shoes 
Agott lent me at the time.

02:08.000 --> 02:10.430
I wanted to fix them up 
before returning them.

02:11.490 --> 02:14.670
I've finished everything except 
the Casting Seal on the soles,

02:14.670 --> 02:17.470
but my lines keep coming out wobbly...

02:18.730 --> 02:23.160
Maybe this isn't the right pen for you?

02:23.580 --> 02:27.900
Different people need 
different weights and grips.

02:27.900 --> 02:29.920
This is just one of my old ones.

02:30.790 --> 02:34.680
Maybe we should have you 
pick one out for yourself?

02:38.050 --> 02:40.460
Coco, let's go to the magic stationer's!

02:40.460 --> 02:41.750
Magic stationer's?

02:41.750 --> 02:44.960
Yes. They stock all kinds 
of magical goods.

02:44.960 --> 02:46.710
It's an art supply store.

02:46.710 --> 02:48.190
An art supply store?

02:48.190 --> 02:49.940
Let's go to the magic stationer's.

02:49.940 --> 02:52.700
M-Magic stationer's?!

02:52.700 --> 02:54.950
It's like a dream!

02:54.950 --> 02:56.700
Coco? Hello?

02:56.700 --> 03:00.130
It's still sinking in. 
Just give me a moment.

04:46.470 --> 04:51.350
<b>Meetings in Kalhn</b>

04:46.760 --> 04:49.170
That's Kalhn, Township of the Marshwoods.

04:49.170 --> 04:50.580
It's that island on the sandbar,

04:50.580 --> 04:53.780
and it's the closest witches' 
town to where we live.

05:03.850 --> 05:05.700
Wait for me!

05:05.700 --> 05:07.950
So, the Casting Seal to 
make your skirt fuller...

05:07.950 --> 05:10.460
My wand's finally taking 
the ink properly, so...

05:10.460 --> 05:12.460
So many witches...

05:13.010 --> 05:19.470
To protect the city from the molewyrms 
in the Marshwoods on the far bank,

05:19.470 --> 05:22.830
the witches built part of the sandbar 
into an island to support a watchtower.

05:23.340 --> 05:26.320
Witches started to gather here, 
it grew into an atelier town,

05:26.320 --> 05:28.720
and they haven't even 
built a bridge to it...

05:26.660 --> 05:29.210
Master Qifrey, Coco's not listening!

05:29.210 --> 05:30.100
Excuse me.

05:30.360 --> 05:34.360
I have better things to do 
than play tour guide for Coco.

05:34.360 --> 05:36.210
I'm going off on my own.

05:36.210 --> 05:37.770
There are shops I want to visit.

05:37.770 --> 05:40.370
We'll meet up at the magic stationer's!

05:42.260 --> 05:45.240
How are things going with Agott?

05:46.120 --> 05:47.530
Well...

05:47.990 --> 05:50.440
I really wish we could be closer.

06:04.210 --> 06:05.830
Hey!

06:06.970 --> 06:08.730
We're over here!

06:15.390 --> 06:18.110
It's like a dream!

06:35.830 --> 06:37.200
Coco!

06:37.200 --> 06:39.760
We're not supposed to get separated!

06:45.150 --> 06:47.490
Kalhn's just <i>full</i> of people, isn't it?

06:47.490 --> 06:49.910
I'm tired.

06:50.900 --> 06:54.300
This is the magic stationer's, 
the Starry Sword.

07:18.900 --> 07:21.280
There's a tree growing through 
the middle of the shop...

07:21.610 --> 07:23.090
Well, well.

07:23.440 --> 07:28.840
I don't often see a witch's apprentice 
wonderstruck by a Silverwood Tree.

07:30.800 --> 07:34.220
You really don't know 
something so elementary?

07:34.220 --> 07:35.820
Don't be like that.

07:35.820 --> 07:38.780
Coco hasn't been an apprentice for long.

07:40.730 --> 07:43.160
Then this is the famous...

07:45.190 --> 07:47.860
Well, that does explain it!

07:47.860 --> 07:50.720
Do forgive me, dearie.

07:50.720 --> 07:54.960
I didn't recognize you either, so... 
I guess that makes us even!

07:57.250 --> 07:59.000
This is Mister Nolnoa!

07:59.000 --> 08:02.120
He's the owner of the magic 
stationer's, the Starry Sword!

08:02.120 --> 08:03.250
Indeed.

08:03.560 --> 08:09.000
All the Components here were made 
by me and my grandson Tartah.

08:09.000 --> 08:11.330
All the pens, all the ink...

08:11.330 --> 08:13.660
Every last one!

08:13.660 --> 08:17.190
I can also extract Conjuring Ink 
at whatever concentration you want.

08:17.190 --> 08:18.650
Extract...?

08:21.820 --> 08:23.160
Coco, was it?

08:23.160 --> 08:25.820
I'll show you. Come along, now.

08:25.820 --> 08:26.790
Yes, sir!

09:19.950 --> 09:21.520
It turned black!

09:21.520 --> 09:23.330
That's Woodcruor.

09:23.330 --> 09:26.420
The branches are a silvery white 
when they're healthy,

09:26.420 --> 09:28.840
but turn black when they die.

09:29.460 --> 09:34.400
It's toxic in that state, 
both to the tree and to humans.

09:34.840 --> 09:39.890
But once we dissolve it in water, 
then strain out the excess...

09:41.640 --> 09:47.090
We've got ourselves crude Conjuring Ink, 
the source of all magic.

09:49.500 --> 09:54.380
Regular ink is made from the soot that's 
produced when you burn normal wood,

09:54.380 --> 09:56.030
but Conjuring Ink is different.

09:56.030 --> 09:59.400
It's made from the cruor—
the literal "blood"—of the tree.

09:59.960 --> 10:04.980
So Silverwoods are extremely 
important trees to witches.

10:05.290 --> 10:06.900
Yes indeed!

10:06.900 --> 10:10.300
For some reason, it's the only tree 
from which we can extract the ink.

10:10.300 --> 10:11.990
It sounds like an amazing tree!

10:11.990 --> 10:13.200
A precious tree.

10:13.200 --> 10:16.430
That's right! There's an 
old legend about it, too!

10:16.900 --> 10:19.560
Yes, the legend says that long ago,

10:19.560 --> 10:24.700
a Silverwood tree fell 
in love with a witch!

10:24.700 --> 10:28.410
It offered its blood to be ink, 
and its branches to be wands...

10:28.410 --> 10:29.150
Wands?

10:31.150 --> 10:34.000
So, did you come here to buy a wand?

10:34.000 --> 10:34.910
Yes!

10:42.390 --> 10:43.470
Well, then...

10:44.460 --> 10:46.180
Go test a few out.

10:53.720 --> 10:55.900
Use this to do it.

10:58.350 --> 11:02.100
I'm sure you'll find the perfect wand.

11:06.680 --> 11:08.670
What should we go for?

11:08.670 --> 11:11.680
I like lighter wands myself!

11:11.680 --> 11:13.030
I wonder which I should try...

11:18.640 --> 11:20.310
W-Wait!

11:24.930 --> 11:26.000
Coco?

11:27.170 --> 11:29.020
Wh-What do we do?

11:29.020 --> 11:30.000
Don't know.

11:30.000 --> 11:32.800
But she'll get lost if we 
leave her on her own.

11:32.800 --> 11:34.360
We have to find her!

11:46.510 --> 11:47.310
What?!

11:48.120 --> 11:49.350
Agott!

11:49.890 --> 11:51.370
What's going on?

11:54.320 --> 11:55.660
Come with us!

11:55.660 --> 11:57.280
H-Hang on!

11:58.670 --> 12:00.240
What's this all about?

12:28.480 --> 12:30.560
Coco! Come back!

12:33.570 --> 12:35.370
Wait up, Coco!

12:51.650 --> 12:53.120
What are you doing, Coco?

12:53.120 --> 12:54.510
Where do you think you're going?

12:54.510 --> 12:56.200
I... I saw that person!

12:56.200 --> 12:58.580
The one who gave me 
the forbidden magic book!

12:58.580 --> 12:59.760
That witch...

13:02.260 --> 13:03.450
What?

13:03.450 --> 13:05.770
What a ridiculous wild goose chase.

13:05.770 --> 13:08.110
But at least we stayed together!

13:08.110 --> 13:10.050
C'mon, let's go back to the shop!

13:10.050 --> 13:10.890
Hey.

13:11.720 --> 13:15.900
The scenery's too different here 
for us to just be one alley down.

13:16.230 --> 13:17.780
The brushbuddy's gone, too.

13:18.500 --> 13:19.960
You may be right.

13:20.700 --> 13:23.260
It looks completely different.

13:26.900 --> 13:31.040
The walls and floors are made of 
a white stone you don't see in Kalhn.

13:32.170 --> 13:33.540
Which means...

13:33.540 --> 13:35.790
this isn't Kalhn.

13:36.920 --> 13:38.750
Th-That can't be true!

13:38.750 --> 13:42.480
We didn't pass through a Windowway, 
and it's not like we could just teleport!

13:42.480 --> 13:45.170
I'll just have a look from above!

13:46.640 --> 13:49.370
Tetia may be on the right track.

13:50.560 --> 13:54.560
We could have been directly 
teleported without realizing it.

13:55.660 --> 13:58.650
But spells like that 
aren't allowed, right?

13:58.650 --> 14:00.440
That would be...

14:00.760 --> 14:02.350
Forbidden magic.

14:03.200 --> 14:04.900
Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh, no!

14:04.900 --> 14:06.830
This is totally <i>not</i> Kalhn!

14:06.830 --> 14:08.300
We gotta get out of here!

14:08.300 --> 14:09.460
Wait a minute!

14:09.460 --> 14:11.200
Tetia, what's wrong?

14:11.200 --> 14:13.270
Tetia, calm down!

14:13.270 --> 14:14.710
What exactly did you see?

14:14.710 --> 14:18.180
It's less what I saw 
and more what saw <i>me</i>!

14:19.800 --> 14:23.020
I have no business with the others, but...

14:36.770 --> 14:41.040
Coco, welcome to the world of magic.

14:45.140 --> 14:49.030
You are our hope.

14:50.800 --> 14:54.410
Mr. Nolnoa, have you seen my apprentices?

14:54.410 --> 14:56.020
Oh?

14:56.020 --> 14:58.290
I assumed they got bored 
and went for a walk.

14:58.290 --> 14:59.700
How could they get bored?!

14:59.700 --> 15:02.050
This is the best store in the whole town!

15:02.050 --> 15:03.800
I could spend all day browsing in here!

15:03.800 --> 15:06.050
Shucks, I'm blushing!

15:06.500 --> 15:11.260
They're also not the sort of girls 
who'd run off without thanking you.

15:11.680 --> 15:13.160
Where could they be?

15:13.530 --> 15:15.290
I saw them.

15:15.900 --> 15:19.560
They ran after a strangely dressed witch.

15:19.890 --> 15:23.290
The witch had a mask that 
looked like an eyeball...

15:35.450 --> 15:36.680
Stay as you are.

15:37.110 --> 15:41.040
Maintain eye contact 
and back up very slowly.

15:41.520 --> 15:42.880
Once we're far enough,

15:42.880 --> 15:45.280
I'll give the word, 
then we'll run with all our might.

15:56.580 --> 15:57.900
Steady...

15:58.840 --> 16:00.170
Steady...

16:06.820 --> 16:08.010
Now!

16:23.480 --> 16:25.380
Now's our chance! Run!

16:33.050 --> 16:35.250
Agott, that spell was amazing!

16:35.250 --> 16:36.210
Was it a fire spell?!

16:36.210 --> 16:39.340
It used the Sigil of Fire surrounded 
by the Sign of Spiraling Wind.

16:39.340 --> 16:41.430
And you drew it that fast?!

16:41.430 --> 16:42.530
Of course not!

16:43.100 --> 16:45.710
You draw the spells in advance 
in your Palm Quire,

16:45.710 --> 16:49.610
then you can use them in a second 
just by closing the ring!

16:49.610 --> 16:52.220
You're amazing, Agott! So cool!

16:52.220 --> 16:54.620
Do you even realize the danger we're in?!

16:55.250 --> 16:56.620
Agott!

16:56.620 --> 16:59.040
Awful news! We hit a dead end!

16:59.800 --> 17:01.040
Should we take another path?

17:06.070 --> 17:08.010
Wh-What do we do?

17:08.010 --> 17:11.020
The dragon's going to 
track us down and eat us...

17:14.350 --> 17:16.180
I don't want to die.

17:17.130 --> 17:20.850
I haven't left a single 
spell to the world!

17:20.850 --> 17:22.980
Why did this have to—

17:32.230 --> 17:34.290
Tetia, get a grip.

17:34.290 --> 17:36.620
We're witch apprentices.

17:37.200 --> 17:39.140
We'll find a way out with our magic.

17:44.110 --> 17:47.210
I'll use a Wall Breaker spell 
to create an escape hatch.

17:47.210 --> 17:49.170
Richeh, Tetia, buy us time.

17:49.170 --> 17:49.940
Right.

17:49.940 --> 17:50.970
Understood.

17:50.970 --> 17:52.190
There.

17:52.190 --> 17:53.780
Where should I draw it?

17:53.780 --> 17:54.960
Around here, maybe...

17:54.960 --> 17:56.640
Add the signs to this sigil...

17:56.640 --> 17:58.970
Hey, Agott. Check this out!

17:58.970 --> 18:03.710
I think a Casting Seal like this 
should buy us enough time.

17:58.970 --> 18:03.050
<i>I saw it in her eyes. 
She blames me for this.</i>

18:03.710 --> 18:06.630
Yes, that should do it.

18:07.110 --> 18:09.860
<i>But... she's right to.</i>

18:17.620 --> 18:18.860
Please...

18:21.500 --> 18:22.910
Fly!

18:31.860 --> 18:34.070
That should buy us a little time.

18:34.070 --> 18:35.860
Well done, Tetia.

18:35.860 --> 18:36.850
Nice.

18:37.300 --> 18:39.600
Tetia's amazing.

18:47.960 --> 18:49.000
Is that...

18:49.760 --> 18:51.440
Hey, Agott!

18:54.500 --> 18:55.830
I'm sorry! I...

18:56.870 --> 18:58.550
What is wrong with you?!

18:58.550 --> 19:00.240
You don't touch someone 
while they're drawing!

19:00.240 --> 19:02.250
I'm sorry! I didn't do it on purpose!

19:02.250 --> 19:04.120
Didn't do it on purpose?!

19:04.120 --> 19:05.500
Yes, I'm sure you didn't!

19:05.500 --> 19:10.300
Turning your mother into stone, 
putting us in danger...

19:10.300 --> 19:12.760
You didn't mean to do 
any of it, did you?!

19:12.760 --> 19:15.010
But it's all still your fault, Coco!

19:15.360 --> 19:17.730
Get it through your head 
how ignorant you are,

19:17.730 --> 19:19.510
and just stop doing anything!

19:23.640 --> 19:25.520
Wh-What do we do?

19:26.040 --> 19:28.430
I don't have time to start over.

19:28.430 --> 19:30.620
We'll have to go back and find another—

19:30.620 --> 19:31.690
I've got it.

19:40.940 --> 19:43.290
Amazing. Great work, Richeh.

19:43.290 --> 19:45.720
Let's put this dead end behind us.

19:49.750 --> 19:51.920
I meant this part of the maze...

19:53.220 --> 19:57.130
though you can take it 
either way you want to.

20:01.400 --> 20:02.580
Tetia.

20:27.440 --> 20:32.260
<i>Master Qifrey, what should I do?</i>

20:38.540 --> 20:40.090
Qifrey!

20:40.400 --> 20:42.190
Any sign of the girls?

20:44.180 --> 20:47.730
No, they're not anywhere 
outside, at least.

20:48.390 --> 20:49.730
I didn't expect...

20:50.030 --> 20:53.360
that the Brimmed Caps would 
make contact themselves.

20:53.360 --> 20:54.360
Wait!

20:58.160 --> 21:00.250
That was one of the Brimmed Caps?

21:00.250 --> 21:03.570
I wouldn't have dreamed 
one would come here!

21:05.340 --> 21:09.530
A dangerous faction that 
wears hats from a bygone era

21:09.530 --> 21:12.190
and hides their faces behind masks.

21:13.830 --> 21:16.840
<i>I thought Coco would afford us a clue,</i>

21:17.170 --> 21:19.720
<i>but I didn't expect them to come to her.</i>

21:21.860 --> 21:24.980
Tartah, do you remember anything else?

21:24.980 --> 21:25.970
Anything at all?

21:26.730 --> 21:29.170
Um, I'm really sorry.

21:29.170 --> 21:30.730
I don't remember much.

21:31.050 --> 21:32.100
I see.

21:33.480 --> 21:34.980
Wait, you're...

21:41.380 --> 21:43.490
You're the brushbuddy 
that Coco brought back.

21:43.900 --> 21:45.790
Were you with them?

21:47.250 --> 21:48.490
Do you know where they went?

21:57.960 --> 21:59.690
<i>It'll be getting dark soon.</i>

22:00.690 --> 22:02.160
<i>Please, everyone...</i>

22:02.820 --> 22:04.170
<i>Be safe!</i>

23:35.440 --> 23:39.980
Episode 5:

23:35.440 --> 23:39.980
The Dragon's Labyrinth
